WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.591
Read the sentence: the animal crossed the street because it

00:00:03.591 --> 00:00:05.386
was tired. To interpret it,

00:00:05.386 --> 00:00:07.900
you connect that word back to animal.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:11.490
Self-attention gives a model a way to learn connections like

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:14.363
this. Each token gathers information from other tokens,

00:00:14.363 --> 00:00:16.517
with different weights for different relationships.

00:00:16.517 --> 00:00:18.238
Each token produces a query,

00:00:18.238 --> 00:00:19.959
a key, and a value.

00:00:19.959 --> 00:00:23.402
The query is compared with the keys to score possible

00:00:23.402 --> 00:00:26.844
connections. Softmax turns those scores into weights that add up

00:00:26.844 --> 00:00:30.287
to one. A weighted sum of the values gives the

00:00:30.287 --> 00:00:31.664
token its new representation.

00:00:31.684 --> 00:00:35.205
A single set of weights gives one view of a

00:00:35.205 --> 00:00:38.374
sentence. The Transformer runs several attention heads in parallel,

00:00:38.374 --> 00:00:40.487
each with its own learned projections.

00:00:40.487 --> 00:00:44.008
It concatenates their outputs and mixes them with a learned

00:00:44.008 --> 00:00:47.529
matrix, so one token can incorporate several kinds of information.

00:00:47.529 --> 00:00:51.890
Earlier recurrent translation models processed a sentence one position at

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:56.252
a time. The Transformer encoder computes representations for all positions

00:00:56.252 --> 00:00:57.996
in a layer together.

00:00:57.996 --> 00:01:00.613
In the paper's English-to-German translation experiment,

00:01:00.613 --> 00:01:02.794
the model reached 28.4 BLEU.

00:01:02.794 --> 00:01:07.155
The decoder still generates translated words one at a time.
